// Data personages: the figures a campaign seats in place of procedural
// rulers and leaders when its start year is in a row's era window
// (docs/p5d-conflict-world-design.md §B, §H). Typed against
// src/domain/personage_data.zig `Table`.
//
// Source: `canon` rows restate BattleTech setting facts for 3025 (names,
// offices, seats, family ties) in project words, as summarized by
// BattleTechWiki (sarna.net); no text is copied. `authored` rows are
// project fiction. Motives and ambition are project characterization on
// every row. `provenance` is internal metadata and is never displayed.
//
//   key              stable key a save stores (personage.key); never renamed
//   role             planetary_ruler | faction_leader | heir | family | intelligence_chief
//   first_name, last_name, title   display text (markup-safe)
//   faction_key      a factions.zon key
//   seat_planet_key  a planets.zon key: the world ruled, the leader's
//                    capital, or where the figure is placed
//   family_key       a `families` key, or "" for none; rows sharing one are kin
//   motives          two or three distinct motives (§B)
//   ambition         0..politics.ambition_max
//   era_from_year, era_to_year     inclusive start years that seat the row
//   provenance       canon | authored
//
// The build refuses a duplicate or malformed key, an unknown faction, seat
// or family, a ruler off a hiring world of its faction, a leader off its
// faction's capital, two rows on one seat in overlapping windows, an
// out-of-range motive set or ambition, a window not covering 3025, an
// empty or markup-bearing name or title, and a full name the names.zon
// pools could draw.
.{
    .families = .{
        .{ .key = "davion", .name = "House Davion" },
        .{ .key = "steiner", .name = "House Steiner" },
        .{ .key = "kurita", .name = "House Kurita" },
        .{ .key = "liao", .name = "House Liao" },
        .{ .key = "marik", .name = "House Marik" },
    },
